WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.460
SMARTPHONE SHUTDOWN:
LG is one of the most iconic brands in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:21.000
the world as they produce everything from washers&nbsp;
and dryers to smartphones and TVs. For decades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.940
they were the pride and joy of South Korea along&nbsp;
with Samsung, and they still very much hold that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:32.400
status within the country. But, outside of&nbsp;
South Korea, LG has had a rough couple of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:38.820
years especially with smartphones. For years, LG&nbsp;
was trying to break into the smartphone space and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:46.140
establish themselves like Samsung and Apple. But,&nbsp;
year after year, LG walked away with a bigger and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:54.240
bigger loss. During the worst of it, LG was down&nbsp;
$4.5 billion within a matter of just 6 years. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:01:00.120
the reality was that they could only justify such&nbsp;
losses for so long and eventually they wanted out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:06.480
so they started looking for buyers. But, no one&nbsp;
wanted a money pit that needed to compete against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:13.140
Apple and Samsung. So, with no choice left, LG&nbsp;
decided to make the hard decision to completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:20.400
scrap their smartphone business in April of 2021.&nbsp;
But, LG’s outlook wasn’t always so pessimistic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:26.580
At one point, it seemed like LG was here to&nbsp;
stay given their massive presence. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:33.360
LG became the world’s third largest smartphone&nbsp;
maker back in 2013, and they held this title&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:39.480
within North America until the day they shutdown.&nbsp;
And it’s not like LG was stagnating or getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:44.940
too comfortable either. If anything, they were&nbsp;
doing the exact opposite as they were constantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:50.940
innovating and taking chances. In fact, LG was&nbsp;
actually the first company to make a capacitive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:56.640
touchscreen phone way back in 2006. They followed&nbsp;
this up with flexible OLED displays in 2014,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.720
modular smartphones in 2016, ultra wide&nbsp;
cameras in 2016, dual screen phones in 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:07.380
and swivel phones in 2020. We should also note&nbsp;
that LG wasn’t set on trying to maximize profits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.400
and screw over customers either. They not&nbsp;
only kept the headphone jack for 1-2 years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:15.900
longer than everyone else, but they even&nbsp;
tried improving it by integrating a Quad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:21.000
DAC into their phones. From the outside, it&nbsp;
seemed like LG had literally everything going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:26.340
for them. They were a household name with&nbsp;
a bunch resources and they were constantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:33.300
trying to outdo not just the competition&nbsp;
but themselves. So, what happened to LG?

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:42.240
NON EXISTENT MARKETING:
Taking a look back, LG’s eventual demise can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:48.300
be traced back to their very first “smartphone”:&nbsp;
the LG Prada back in December of 2006. As we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:52.980
previously touched on, the Prada was the first&nbsp;
phone to ever have a capacitive touchscreen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:59.700
and LG was even suspicious that Apple had ripped&nbsp;
off their design. But, you’ve probably never even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:05.580
heard of this phone which brings us into LG’s&nbsp;
number one mistake: non existent marketing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:11.160
This was likely a trait that LG brought with them&nbsp;
from the appliance space. With refrigerators and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:18.120
washers, marketing is not exactly one of your top&nbsp;
concerns. For most people, these are necessities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.662
that they only buy when their old ones break.&nbsp;
You know, it’s not everyday that you think:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.662 --> 00:03:20.763
Woah LG just dropped their latest dishwasher. I&nbsp;
better put in a preorder before it’s too late. No,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.763 --> 00:03:22.740
with appliances, the key isn’t over the top&nbsp;
marketing. The key is strong availability,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:28.740
offering great value, and having a reputation&nbsp;
for reliability. Practicality sells appliances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:34.260
not showmanship. LG approached the smartphone&nbsp;
market with the same mentality. They figured that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:39.360
if they could just make a strong product, people&nbsp;
would be lining up to buy their phones. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.920
the key difference between appliances and&nbsp;
smartphones was that one was a necessity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:49.800
and the other was a luxury atleast back in the&nbsp;
day. With smartphones, people wanted something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:56.040
that was desired, something that was exclusive,&nbsp;
something that gave them social status. Apple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:01.140
offered exactly this. They had their massive&nbsp;
keynotes that garnered tens of millions of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:07.020
views. Even if you had no intention of buying an&nbsp;
iPhone, you knew about the new one that Apple just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:13.020
released. And the people who wanted them? Well,&nbsp;
some of them would wait for literal days outside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:18.540
Apple stores to be the first ones to get the new&nbsp;
iPhone. What did LG do on the other hand? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:24.480
they dropped smartphones as if they were iOS&nbsp;
updates. Actually, no wait, I take that back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:29.820
iOS updates actually get more press. The LG&nbsp;
launch events took place during Korea time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:35.280
which made it hard for western audiences to tune&nbsp;
in. But, it wouldn’t matter even if they did tune&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:40.620
in given that LG didn’t build any tension or&nbsp;
hype. Their phones would become available in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:46.620
Korea the exact same day. Also, there wasn’t any&nbsp;
sort of synchronized international launch. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:50.880
launch dates for America and Europe were simply&nbsp;
when logistics channels could get them there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:57.240
and oftentimes, this was months. Again, this seems&nbsp;
to be a lingering attribute of their appliance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:02.520
business. People don’t hold out on buying a stove&nbsp;
because a new one is just around the corner. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:06.960
the specifics of when a new product made it’s&nbsp;
way to western markets didn’t really matter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:13.500
With smartphones, however, people want the latest&nbsp;
and greatest. In fact, many people hold out for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:19.200
several months just so they can get the latest&nbsp;
right when it drops. I know you’re watching. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:23.640
much of LG’s success in the smartphone space in&nbsp;
the early days simply came from the fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:28.740
they were already an established cellphone maker&nbsp;
and brand. But, other than that, they didn’t have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:33.480
much going for them, and when more competition&nbsp;
entered the scene, they would feel the squeeze.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:40.440
GIMMICKS:
As the smartphone market continued to mature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:45.780
we started to see smartphones transition from&nbsp;
being a luxury to being a necessity. This gave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:50.640
rise to a whole new demographic of people who&nbsp;
were just looking for a practical value device.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:56.520
Companies like Google, OnePlus, Xiaomi, and Huawei&nbsp;
have basically built their entire smartphone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:03.120
business around this market. You would think that&nbsp;
this was the perfect opportunity for LG. They were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:08.820
already in the space making practical devices, so&nbsp;
all they had to do was double down and pump out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:15.300
some marketing about how much value they offer.&nbsp;
But, LG obviously didn’t do that. You see, in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:21.900
2012 and 2013, LG finally realized their marketing&nbsp;
blunder. They needed to make LG smartphones the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:28.260
latest and greatest, and they needed to make them&nbsp;
unique, special, and exclusive. With that in mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:34.320
they decided to go after the premium market&nbsp;
which isn’t a bad thing. LG had a shot at taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:41.280
on Samsung and maybe even overtaking them, but&nbsp;
while LG had the right idea, they also kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:46.920
didn’t. LG was right in that they had to offer&nbsp;
the latest and greatest. But, they were wrong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:51.900
in thinking that they actually had to make the&nbsp;
latest and greatest. Whether we’re talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:58.620
Mercedes or Apple, the key to making the latest&nbsp;
and greatest isn’t to actually make the latest and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:04.320
greatest. The key is to make a strong product&nbsp;
and pair it with exceptional positioning. LG,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:09.780
however, approached this from a literal sense and&nbsp;
incorporated some wacky stuff into their phones.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:16.080
A few of their experiments actually turned out to&nbsp;
be trend setting. For example, the LG G5 was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:22.080
first smartphone to sport an ultrawide camera way&nbsp;
back in 2016. Since then, ultrawide cameras have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:27.360
become a standard amongst premium smartphones.&nbsp;
But, most of LG’s experiments didn’t play out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:34.080
quite as well starting with the LG G Flex in 2013.&nbsp;
Around this time, curved TVs were a hot thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:40.140
so LG figured that they should bring this feature&nbsp;
to smartphones. But, this choice ended up aging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:47.160
as well as curved TVs themselves. Soon after,&nbsp;
we saw the LG V10 in 2015. This phone came with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:53.520
two unique features. One, the phone had two front&nbsp;
facing cameras, and two, the phone had a secondary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:59.160
screen at the top that displayed a taskbar type of&nbsp;
thing that never really caught on. Moving forward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:05.580
we saw the LG G5 in 2016. The selling feature&nbsp;
of this phone was the fact that it was modular.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:10.500
During a time when everyone was following the&nbsp;
Apple way and preventing smartphone upgrades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:16.140
LG decided to give choice back to the consumers.&nbsp;
But, LG’s partners never pulled through and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:21.660
put out accessories that made the modularity&nbsp;
actually worthwhile. Nonetheless, LG continued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:26.520
pushing forward. They introduced a dual screen&nbsp;
phone with the G8X and a swivel phone with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:32.580
LG Wing. But while these features made LG phones&nbsp;
as expensive as iPhones, they didn’t make them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:38.760
as appealing as iPhones. LG simply became known&nbsp;
as the smartphone producer with the gimmicks.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:46.440
GETTING DESPERATE:
As losses continued to pile up at LG, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:52.320
naturally became more desperate. Their gimmicks&nbsp;
became more outrageous and their focus became more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:57.960
tunnel visioned. Everything centered around: how&nbsp;
do we get more attention and how do we sell more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:04.080
units. This makes sense given that volume was by&nbsp;
far their biggest pain point. They simply weren’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:10.080
able to sell enough units to make up for their&nbsp;
monster R&amp;D expenses. So, they naturally shifted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:15.900
all their focus into garnering more sales. From a&nbsp;
macro perspective, this was a great choice given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:22.140
that this is exactly what LG had been lacking for&nbsp;
so long. But, unfortunately this came with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:27.900
cost of sacrificing current users. LG started to&nbsp;
drop the ball when it came to software, hardware,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:34.680
and UI optimization. For example, while LG phones&nbsp;
had massive batteries on the spec sheet, the real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:40.500
world performance was average at best due to the&nbsp;
phones being so inefficient. Software updates also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:46.200
became few and far between, and several LG phones&nbsp;
were plagued with bootloop issues. It didn’t take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:51.960
long for LG to become infamous for their software&nbsp;
issues, but these issues didn’t just stop at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:58.500
software. LG started having hardware issues as&nbsp;
well. On the LG V20, for example, the camera glass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:04.680
was for some reason extremely fragile. LG phones&nbsp;
were also plagued with battery overheating issues,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:10.620
microphone issues, network issues, and fingerprint&nbsp;
sensor issues. LG’s whole business was centered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:17.100
around making practical electronics, but somehow,&nbsp;
their new smartphones were anything but practical.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:23.340
And to make things worse, it didn’t seem like LG&nbsp;
was truly trying to fix any of this either. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:28.080
had gone so far down the latest and greatest&nbsp;
rabbit hole that all they seemingly wanted to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:33.660
do was create something that was super out there&nbsp;
and garner the attention of the media. The purpose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:38.700
of their new phones were to simply get you to buy.&nbsp;
They didn’t care about your experience using the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:44.520
phone or your feedback. This strategy may work&nbsp;
alright if your selling products that people only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:50.520
buy once. But, with phones, people are constantly&nbsp;
replacing them every few years. Not to mention,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:56.820
people use their phones for hours every single&nbsp;
day, so it didn’t take them long to notice. LG&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.820 --> 00:11:01.620
did eventually try to make it up to customers&nbsp;
by offering super long warranties. For the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:07.080
phones affected by bootloops for example, LG&nbsp;
offered warranties for up to 30 months. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:11.580
this is not the type of impression that&nbsp;
you can reverse. Once people believe that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:16.920
LG phones offer a crappy experience, they’re&nbsp;
gonna hold that belief forever. And now that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:21.800
even LG’s existing users were turning&nbsp;
on the company, their fate was sealed.

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:26.700
THE STATE OF LG:
In the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:33.180
LG is a perfect example of: just because you’re&nbsp;
successful in one industry doesn’t mean that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:39.300
you’ll be successful in another. Throughout their&nbsp;
entire smartphone run, they were constantly at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:44.220
wrong place at the wrong time. In the early days&nbsp;
when the market was filled with luxury buyers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:50.160
LG’s marketing and positioning simply wasn’t up&nbsp;
to par. Then, when the general market joined the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:55.380
scene, LG finally decided to go after the&nbsp;
premium market, but not strong marketing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.380 --> 00:12:01.980
but with out there gimmicks that rarely hit. And&nbsp;
finally, LG became so desperate on getting new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:08.160
sales that they started completely ignoring their&nbsp;
core market of existing users. With such fatal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:14.400
flaws, it’s no wonder that after 15 years in the&nbsp;
smartphone industry, all LG had to show for it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:19.560
billions of dollars worth of losses and hundreds&nbsp;
of millions of angry customers. Looking forard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:24.960
it doesn’t seem like LG will be restarting&nbsp;
their smartphone business anytime soon. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:30.480
the company is doing better without smartphones,&nbsp;
so it’s probably best that they stick to what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:35.580
they’re good at. But hey, while LG wasn’t able to&nbsp;
make it within the smartphone space themselves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:41.880
we may very well see many of their gimmicks make a&nbsp;
comeback in a much better way, but only time will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:48.240
tell. Did you ever own an LG smartphone? Comment&nbsp;
that down below. Also, drop a like if you hope LG&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:53.100
smartphones rest in peace. And of course, consider&nbsp;
checking out our discord community to suggest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:56.760
future video ideas and consider subscribing&nbsp;
to see more questions logically answered.

